WHAT TO PRODUCE (JSON, fields: {{ schema_fields }}):
1. `title`, `summary` (two sentences), `setting` (place, era, weather, time of day), `mood`.
2. `bounds` — centre + extents in meters of the whole playable area (a garden 30 × 10 × 30 m; a
   harbour 120 × 30 × 120 m). Keep it as small as the brief allows: detail beats acreage.
3. `environment` — ONE paragraph with numbers: sky colours (hex), sun/moon direction as azimuth +
   elevation in degrees, light colour/intensity, fog colour + density, ground material and height,
   water plane height if any.
4. `zones` — 3 to 8 spatial regions with PascalCase names, a description of what is there and how it
   is laid out (paths, clusters, spacing in meters), a `bbox`, and `contents` = asset names placed
   there. Zone bboxes tile the bounds without overlapping by more than 1 m.
5. `assets` — 4 to 12 reusable things placed in zones. PascalCase `name`; `kind` = `threejs` for
   procedural shapes (fences, lanterns, rocks, benches, trees, boats) or `blender_glb` ONLY for 1-3
   hero objects that need sculpted/bevelled detail; `description` with construction numbers and
   colours; `approx_size_m` = width × height × depth in meters (a stone lantern 0.5 × 1.6 × 0.5;
   a bench 1.6 × 0.9 × 0.6; a pine 3 × 7 × 3); `instances_hint` = how many appear in total.
   Ground cover, terrain, water and sky are NOT assets — they belong to the environment / zones.
6. `effects` — 1 to 4: `glsl_material` (water ripple, lantern glow, wind-swayed foliage),
   `particles` (petals, sparks, snow), `animated_geometry`, or `postprocess`; say which zone/asset.
7. `animation` — 2 to 6 lines of what moves: amplitude + frequency in numbers.
8. `cameras` — 2 to 4 authored cameras: `position`, `look_at` (meters), `fov` 35-70, `purpose`
   (establishing shot from outside the bounds looking in; eye level at 1.6-1.8 m inside a zone; a
   detail shot of the hero asset). Every camera must see at least two zones or a hero asset.
9. `acceptance` — 6 to 12 items: each must-have from the brief, the hero assets visible from the
   establishing camera, time-of-day lighting reads correctly, animation visible between t=0 and
   t=1.5 s, no floating or sunken assets (`how: probe`), fps ≥ 30 at 1024×576.

RULES
- Every name in `zones[].contents` must be an asset name; asset names unique; zone names unique.
- Realistic scale: people 1.7 m, doors 2.1 m, steps 0.17 m, benches 0.45 m seat height.
- Prefer ≤ 8 assets and 3-5 zones for modest briefs. No prose outside the JSON.

